        -:   70:/**
        -:   71: * Used to inspect and possibly collect the (search) results of iterating over a list or
        -:   72: * tree of #KICAD_T objects.
        -:   73: *
        -:   74: * Provide an implementation as needed to inspect EDA_ITEMs visited via #EDA_ITEM::Visit()
        -:   75: * and #EDA_ITEM::IterateForward().
        -:   76: *
        -:   77: * FYI the std::function may hold a lambda, std::bind, pointer to func, or ptr to member
        -:   78: * function, per modern C++. It is used primarily for searching, but not limited to that.
        -:   79: * It can also collect or modify the scanned objects.  'Capturing' lambdas are particularly
        -:   80: * convenient because they can use context and this often means @a aTestData is not used.
        -:   81: *
        -:   82: * @param aItem An #EDA_ITEM to examine.
        -:   83: * @param aTestData is arbitrary data needed by the inspector to determine
        -:   84: *  if the EDA_ITEM under test meets its match criteria, and is often NULL
        -:   85: *  with the advent of capturing lambdas.
        -:   86: * @return A #SEARCH_RESULT type #SEARCH_QUIT if the iterator function is to
        -:   87: *          stop the scan, else #SEARCH_CONTINUE;
        -:   88: */
        -:   89:typedef std::function< INSPECT_RESULT ( EDA_ITEM* aItem, void* aTestData ) > INSPECTOR_FUNC;
        -:   90:
        -:   91:/// std::function passed to nested users by ref, avoids copying std::function.
        -:   92:typedef const INSPECTOR_FUNC& INSPECTOR;
